[97.693653, "o", "=== TIMEZONE FIX SUMMARY ===\r\n\r\nPROBLEM:\r\n--------\r\nThe gen_report.py script was generating report filenames with incorrect timestamps.\r\nWhen run from cron (which may have TZ=UTC or no TZ set), the script would use\r\nUTC time instead of the configured Asia/Tokyo timezone, resulting in timestamps\r\nlike 00:00:00 instead of 09:00:00 (9 hour difference).\r\n\r\nROOT CAUSE:\r\n-----------\r\nThe script was reading /etc/timezone and setting os.environ['TZ'], but Python's\r\ndatetime module doesn't automatically pick up TZ environment changes after the\r\nprocess starts. Simply setting os.environ['TZ'] is not enough.\r\n\r\nSOLUTION:\r\n---------\r\nAdded two critical changes to gen_report.py:\r\n1. Import the 'time' module\r\n2. Call time.tzset() immediately after setting os.environ['TZ']\r\n\r\nThis forces Python to reload timezone information and apply the new TZ setting.\r\n\r\nCHANGES MADE:\r\n-------------\r\n- Line 4: Added 'import time'\r\n- Lines 12-13: Added time.tzset() call with explanatory comment\r\n\r\nVERIFICATION:\r\n-------------\r\nTested with"]
[97.693707, "o", " TZ=UTC environment (simulating cron):\r\n- Without fix: datetime.now() returns 17:44:41 (UTC)\r\n- With fix: datetime.now() returns 02:44:41 (JST)\r\n\r\nThe script now correctly generates reports with Asia/Tokyo timestamps regardless\r\nof the environment TZ setting when run from cron.\r\n\r\nBackup of original script saved at: /home/user/scheduler/gen_report.py.backup\r\n"]
[97.693846, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
